---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import BusinessPerspectiveNote from '../../components/BusinessPerspectiveNote.astro';
import ToolNextStep from '../../components/ToolNextStep.astro';
import ScholarshipApplicationPlanner from '../../components/ScholarshipApplicationPlanner.astro';

const title = 'Scholarship Application Planner: Dates and Documents';
const description = 'Turn a scholarship notice into a dated plan with a document checklist and the money you still need. Free, private, copy to WhatsApp.';
const canonical = 'https://futurecareerschool.com/tools/scholarship-application-planner/';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Nav activePage="tools" />
  <BusinessPerspectiveNote />
  <main>
    <section class="tool-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">FREE FUNDING PLANNER</p><h1>Scholarship Application <span>Planner</span></h1><p class="lead">Get your papers and dates ready before the deadline, not after an agent's promise. Enter the scholarship name and last date to get a dated plan and a list of documents still to collect.</p><p class="tool-limits">This tool does not list scholarships or check if you qualify. Use the current official notice, and never pay anyone to be selected.</p></section>
    <section class="container tool-shell"><ScholarshipApplicationPlanner /></section>
    <section class="container tool-explainer"><h2>Keep funding decisions evidence-led</h2><div class="explainer-grid"><article><h3>Check the scheme</h3><p>Save the issuing body, notice, last date, eligibility rules and correction process from an official source.</p></article><article><h3>Prepare readable proof</h3><p>Match every rule to a document, and keep copies of what you submit.</p></article><article><h3>Plan the gap</h3><p>Do not commit to a course assuming an award is guaranteed, renewed or enough for the whole cost.</p></article></div>
    <h2>The National Scholarship Portal (checked 23 November 2026)</h2><p>On 23 November 2026 the home page of <a href="https://scholarships.gov.in">scholarships.gov.in</a> described the National Scholarship Portal as the Government of India portal for 2026-27 applications. It asks students to make a One Time Registration (OTR) using Aadhaar, and it links to guidance on linking a bank account to Aadhaar.</p><p>It also said students with a disability must first log in to the UDID portal and give consent. For a Common Service Centre it listed a fixed fee of ₹30 per student, so be careful if anyone asks for more to select you. Rules change each year, so read the current page yourself, and use your state's portal if your scheme is a state one.</p>
    <h2>A worked example (an illustration, not a real scheme)</h2><p>A first-year student finds a scholarship that closes in 30 days and pays ₹30,000 a year. The plan gives dates for the notice check, the document scans and the submission, and keeps the last fifth of the days spare for portal problems.</p><p>The student's yearly cost is ₹1,20,000, so the award covers 25% and ₹90,000 is still needed. The family now knows to plan that money, and not to pay a deposit on the hope of an award.</p>
    <h2>When to talk to a person</h2><p>If a rule or a document is unclear, ask the scholarship office of your school or college, or the helpline named on the official notice. Do not give your Aadhaar number, OTP or bank password to an agent.</p></section>
    <ToolNextStep toolName="Scholarship Application Planner" audience="student" />
  </main><Footer />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .tool-hero{padding:5rem 1.25rem 2rem}.tool-hero h1{max-width:850px}.tool-hero h1 span{color:var(--gold,#e5b84a)}.lead{max-width:760px;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.7}.tool-limits{max-width:760px;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted,#b9c2c1)}.tool-shell{max-width:1050px}.tool-explainer{padding:2rem 1.25rem 5rem}.tool-explainer h2{margin-top:0}.explainer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.explainer-grid article{padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);border-radius:14px}.explainer-grid h3{margin-top:0}@media(max-width:720px){.tool-hero{padding-top:3rem}.explainer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
